Source: contactci-core
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Contact CI Support <support@contactci.co>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake (>= 3.22),
               ninja-build,
               curl,
Standards-Version: 4.6.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://contactci.co

# The runtime package is named after the SONAME major version (libccic.so.3).
# A major version bump renames it: build.sh --package checks the two agree.
Package: libcontactci-core3
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Contact CI Core client libraries
 Core lets an application use Contact CI haptic gloves. It talks to the
 Contact CI Service (contactci-service) over a local socket and shared memory.
 .
 This package has the shared libraries: libccic, the C API, and libcci, the
 C++ implementation it wraps. Protocol Buffers is linked into libcci.

Package: libcontactci-core-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: libcontactci-core3 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Contact CI Core client libraries (development files)
 Core lets an application use Contact CI haptic gloves. It talks to the
 Contact CI Service (contactci-service) over a local socket and shared memory.
 .
 This package has the headers for the C API (contactci.h) and the unversioned
 libccic.so link to build against.

# The Python binding (python/contactci): pure Python, installed as it is, so it
# needs no Python build tooling (dh-python, pip, setuptools). It is built per
# architecture like the library, not "all": it depends on exactly this build's
# libcontactci-core3, whose headers its ctypes mirrors are tested against, and
# every release file is named and checked per Ubuntu release and architecture.
# A major version bump renames the library package in Depends too:
# python/tests/test_packaging.py checks it.
Package: python3-contactci
Section: python
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), libcontactci-core3 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Contact CI Core client library (Python binding)
 Core lets an application use Contact CI haptic gloves. It talks to the
 Contact CI Service (contactci-service) over a local socket and shared memory.
 .
 This package has contactci, the Python binding over the C API: pure Python
 (ctypes) with no dependencies beyond the standard library. It loads libccic
 from libcontactci-core3 when the first Session opens.
